    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1328">

                <pb facs="1588" n="1390" sameAs="frus:frus1945Berlinv02/pg1390"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.00/7–2045: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 1328<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Iran</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Murray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">restricted</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tehran</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-07-20T13:00:00+03:25">July 20, 1945—1 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>511. Speaking in Majlis yesterday Deputy Ardalan urged early withdrawal British
                    and Soviet troops in accordance Article 5 Tripartite Treaty.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d1328-f1"/> Prime Minister Sadr replied that govt agreed and was
                    studying problem.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Murray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1328-f1" n="1" xml:id="d1328-f1-content">
                <p>i. e., the Anglo-Soviet-Iranian treaty of January 29, 1942. Text in Department of
                    State <hi rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>, vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >vi</hi>, p. 249.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
